### CORRECTION (appended at handoff, 2026-10-19T13:24:16Z)
The base-selftest DIRTY 14/15 above was SELF-INFLICTED: I ran the HEAD blob renamed
as base-tool.py, but selftest case label-utc-render-tz-independent re-spawns the tool
by its canonical name from its own directory (base tool line 733: Path(__file__).resolve().parent / 'custody-pair.py').
Re-run with the canonical filename in the scratch copy dir:
  $ mkdir -p /dev/shm/ex29-beforecol/canon && cp base-tool.py /dev/shm/ex29-beforecol/canon/custody-pair.py
  $ python3 /dev/shm/ex29-beforecol/canon/custody-pair.py selftest --scratch /dev/shm
  CUSTODY_PAIR_SELFTEST: CLEAN cases=15 passed=15 failed=0 exit=0   (base-selftest-exit=0)
So the BEFORE row is 15/15 CLEAN exit 0, as the draft claimed. The landed
before-selftest-base.out (10:18) shows the same self-inflicted DIRTY for the same
reason (its scratch copy at /dev/shm/ex29-base/custody-pair.py was already gone).
Neither is a defect of the base tool.

